From 2a05b904bc048a94993cd30ca98349f3f3f774c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 19:14:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] A3 of the compatibility program, piece 1: the islands and the
 ###Relational dynaFunctions say SQL's SUBSTRING and POSITION by name

Two lite-internal natives, meta::legend::lite::sqlSubstring (a 1-based start and a length) and sqlPosition (1-based,
0 on a miss), each the database's function verbatim -- the same SqlFn.SUBSTRING and STRPOS calls the plain substring
and String indexOf rules emit today -- and the 47 call heads of the #Cypher, #SQL and #IQ islands (CypherToPure 21,
PostgresFunctions 10, IqFunctions 14, IqAggregates 2) and the 3 dynaFunction sites (RelOpTranslator: indexOf,
substring, position) retargeted to them. Pure's own substring and indexOf are then free to take Pure's meaning (A3's
second piece). The islands name the natives by their text (SqlToPure.SQL_SUBSTRING, SQL_POSITION: the protocol layer
cannot import the catalog, as quotient). native-claims.tsv regenerated (bazel run //core:update_generated).

Guard moves NOT made here, pending the user's word in this session: NativeCatalogGovernanceTest's INTERNAL_DESUGAR
ceiling (38 -> 40) and the frontends' text goldens.

Shape: docs/records/compat-homework/A3-shape-note.md (claude/compat-translator-spike), option (a).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0195rQEn5jsUCYS6QSWLrxgF
